the mnu kernel ChangeLog   - version 0.12
    - Release date: 2026-07-17
    - Release creator: tas0dev

Changes:
* Fixed the x86_64 user-mode iretq return path for
  QEMU/KVM by using a conventional flat user data
  descriptor and mapping descriptor tables into
  user CR3 for KPTI trap returns.
* Fixed fork page-table cloning so preinstalled
  per-CPU syscall and descriptor-table mappings are
  not copied as private user pages.
* Fixed TSS RSP0 updates while running on a user CR3
  with read-only descriptor-table mappings.
* Isolated GDT/IDT storage on page boundaries so KPTI
  descriptor mappings do not make unrelated kernel data
  read-only.
* Fixed context switching to update kernel-only CPU
  state after returning to the kernel page table.
* Fixed fork-child user-mode entry to write IA32_FS_BASE
  with the correct MSR selector.
* Reduced boot-time serial output by removing normal
  exec_manifest admission warnings while keeping denial logs.
* Added QEMU/KVM runner support for
  qemu64/single-core defaults.
* Fixed a bug in the filesystem syscall.
* Moved executable signature policy out of
  the kernel.
